# tokio::fs::DirEntry::file_name

Kind: method
Defined in: `tokio::fs::DirEntry`
Signature: `pub fn file_name(&self) -> OsString`

Returns the bare file name of this directory entry without any other
leading path component.

# Examples

```rust
use tokio::fs;

let mut entries = fs::read_dir(".").await?;

while let Some(entry) = entries.next_entry().await? {
    println!("{:?}", entry.file_name());
}
```

# tokio::fs::DirEntry::file_type

Kind: method
Defined in: `tokio::fs::DirEntry`
Signature: `pub async fn file_type(&self) -> Result<FileType>`

Returns the file type for the file that this entry points at.

This function will not traverse symlinks if this entry points at a
symlink.

# Platform-specific behavior

On Windows and most Unix platforms this function is free (no extra
system calls needed), but some Unix platforms may require the equivalent
call to `symlink_metadata` to learn about the target file type.

# Examples

```rust
use tokio::fs;

let mut entries = fs::read_dir(".").await?;

while let Some(entry) = entries.next_entry().await? {
    if let Ok(file_type) = entry.file_type().await {
        // Now let's show our entry's file type!
        println!("{:?}: {:?}", entry.path(), file_type);
    } else {
        println!("Couldn't get file type for {:?}", entry.path());
    }
}
```

# tokio::fs::DirEntry::metadata

Kind: method
Defined in: `tokio::fs::DirEntry`
Signature: `pub async fn metadata(&self) -> Result<Metadata>`

Returns the metadata for the file that this entry points at.

This function will not traverse symlinks if this entry points at a
symlink.

# Platform-specific behavior

On Windows this function is cheap to call (no extra system calls
needed), but on Unix platforms this function is the equivalent of
calling `symlink_metadata` on the path.

# Examples

```rust
use tokio::fs;

let mut entries = fs::read_dir(".").await?;

while let Some(entry) = entries.next_entry().await? {
    if let Ok(metadata) = entry.metadata().await {
        // Now let's show our entry's permissions!
        println!("{:?}: {:?}", entry.path(), metadata.permissions());
    } else {
        println!("Couldn't get file type for {:?}", entry.path());
    }
}
```

